title: "statement gossip: hold initial sync to the peer's statement rate limit"

doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    A node now serves a peer's statement backlog at the rate the peer accepts. Each peer carries
    a mirror of its statement rate limit on the send side: propagation charges it per chunk, and
    an initial sync charges it per statement, cutting a chunk where the quota runs out. A fast
    peer's initial sync no longer pushes it past `statements_per_second`, where it disconnected
    the node as a flooder, and a peer that keeps asking for its backlog draws it at that rate.

crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
